{
  "_readme": [
    "Recorded CPI measurements for the VestaRV core. These are the numbers TRM",
    "Section 12 (\\label{s:cpi}) publishes, and //verification/cpi asserts them",
    "against the RTL on every bazel test run.",
    "",
    "`images` is RAW: four counters per image, taken from the CPIRESULT line",
    "vesta_cpi_tb prints. Each is proven by its own cpi_test target, EXACTLY,",
    "with no tolerance. The simulation is deterministic, so any difference is a",
    "real change in what the core does.",
    "",
    "Everything else is DERIVED from `images` by the same arithmetic the TRM",
    "prints, and is recorded so a reader can diff this file against the TRM by",
    "eye. derived_tables_test.py proves the derived half follows from the raw",
    "half; it needs no simulation, so it covers the manual long-benchmark",
    "images too.",
    "",
    "RE-RECORDING. A DELIBERATE core change re-records this file IN THE SAME",
    "COMMIT as the RTL change, together with the affected tables of TRM",
    "Section 12. The counts, the RTL and the document move as one, so a CPI",
    "change is always visible in the diff and drift is never silent. A failing",
    "target here is therefore either a regression or an un-recorded intentional",
    "change; it is never noise. See verification/cpi/README.md."
  ],
  "harness": {
    "testbench": "verification/cpi/vesta_cpi_tb.vhd",
    "simulator": "@ghdl//:ghdl, --std=08 -fsynopsys, mcode backend",
    "toolchain": "@xpack_riscv_gcc, xPack riscv-none-elf-gcc 13.2.0-2",
    "march": "rv32imac_zicsr_zba_zbb_zbc_zbs",
    "march_noc": "rv32ima_zicsr_zba_zbb_zbc_zbs",
    "benchmark_opts": "-O2 -ffast-math -DPREALLOCATE=1, see //verification/cpi:defs.bzl",
    "measured_region": "the setStats() kernel window, so startup, the PREALLOCATE warm-up pass and result verification are excluded",
    "cycle_source": "the free-running clk, so a cycle with the core clock gated is still charged",
    "instruction_source": "dut.inst_retired, the same predicate csr_unit increments minstret on",
    "trm_section": "platform/common/latex/TRM.template.tex, \\section{Core Performance and Instruction Timing}, \\label{s:cpi}"
  },
